window.ScripturaLexicons.BDAG_PART_0292 = {"source":"BDAG","searchAnchorId":"bdag-search-anchor","entryAnchorId":"bdag-entry-anchor","rowsHtml":"<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0292-01\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πόλις, εως, ἡ substantivo feminino cidade, povoação, habitantes BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πόλις, εως, ἡ</td><td>substantivo feminino</td><td>cidade, povoação, habitantes</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0292-02\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πολιτάρχης, ου, ὁ substantivo masculino politarca, magistrado municipal BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πολιτάρχης, ου, ὁ</td><td>substantivo masculino</td><td>politarca, magistrado municipal</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0292-03\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πολιτεία, ας, ἡ substantivo feminino cidadania, Estado, povo, conduta BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πολιτεία, ας, ἡ</td><td>substantivo feminino</td><td>cidadania, Estado, povo, conduta</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0292-04\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πολίτευμα, ατος, τό substantivo neutro comunidade política, Estado BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πολίτευμα, ατος, τό</td><td>substantivo neutro</td><td>comunidade política, Estado</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0292-05\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πολιτεύομαι verbo ser cidadão, governar, viver, conduzir-se BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πολιτεύομαι</td><td>verbo</td><td>ser cidadão, governar, viver, conduzir-se</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0292-06\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πολίτης, ου, ὁ substantivo masculino cidadão, concidadão, compatriota BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πολίτης, ου, ὁ</td><td>substantivo masculino</td><td>cidadão, concidadão, compatriota</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0292-07\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πολῖτις, ιδος, ἡ substantivo feminino cidadã BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πολῖτις, ιδος, ἡ</td><td>substantivo feminino</td><td>cidadã</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0292-08\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πολλά remissão ver πολύς BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πολλά</td><td>remissão</td><td>ver πολύς</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0292-09\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πολλάκις advérbio muitas vezes, frequentemente BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πολλάκις</td><td>advérbio</td><td>muitas vezes, frequentemente</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0292-10\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πολλαπλασιάζω verbo multiplicar, aumentar BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πολλαπλασιάζω</td><td>verbo</td><td>multiplicar, aumentar</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0292-11\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πολλαπλασίων, ον, adjetivo muitas vezes mais, multiplicado BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πολλαπλασίων, ον,</td><td>adjetivo</td><td>muitas vezes mais, multiplicado</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0292-12\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πολλοστός, ή, όν adjetivo abundante, copioso BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πολλοστός, ή, όν</td><td>adjetivo</td><td>abundante, copioso</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0292-13\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πόλος, ου, ὁ substantivo masculino abóbada celeste, firmamento BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πόλος, ου, ὁ</td><td>substantivo masculino</td><td>abóbada celeste, firmamento</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0292-14\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πολυαγάπητος, ον adjetivo muito amado BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πολυαγάπητος, ον</td><td>adjetivo</td><td>muito amado</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0292-15\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"Πολύβιος, ου, ὁ nome próprio masculino Políbio BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">Πολύβιος, ου, ὁ</td><td>nome próprio masculino</td><td>Políbio</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0292-16\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πολυευσπλαγχνία, ας, ἡ substantivo feminino abundância de misericórdia BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πολυευσπλαγχνία, ας, ἡ</td><td>substantivo feminino</td><td>abundância de misericórdia</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0292-17\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πολυεύσπλαγχνος, ον adjetivo rico em compaixão BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πολυεύσπλαγχνος, ον</td><td>adjetivo</td><td>rico em compaixão</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0292-18\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πολυεύτακτος, ον adjetivo muito bem ordenado, disciplinado BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πολυεύτακτος, ον</td><td>adjetivo</td><td>muito bem ordenado, disciplinado</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0292-19\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"Πολύκαρπος, ου, ὁ nome próprio masculino Policarpo BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">Πολύκαρπος, ου, ὁ</td><td>nome próprio masculino</td><td>Policarpo</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0292-20\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πολύλαλος, ον adjetivo falador, loquaz, tagarela BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πολύλαλος, ον</td><td>adjetivo</td><td>falador, loquaz, tagarela</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>","cardsHtml":"<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0292-01\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πόλις, εως, ἡ</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>substantivo feminino</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πόλις</span>, <span class=\"greek\">εως</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> (Hom.+. Em geral, um centro populacional em contraste com uma área relativamente desabitada ou rural. No mundo greco-romano, o termo geralmente implicava fortes associações políticas, especialmente no sentido de ‘cidade-Estado’).</p><p class=\"entry-text\">① Centro populacional de tamanho variável, cidade, povoação, lit. <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.5.14\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 5:14</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/LUK.10.8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Lk 10:8</a>, 10. Pl. <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.11.20\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 11:20</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/LUK.5.12\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Lk 5:12</a>; 19:17, 19. <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πόλις</span> a cidade ou povoação designada no contexto <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.8.33\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 8:33</a>; 21:17f; 26:18; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MRK.11.19\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mk 11:19</a>; 14:13, 16; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/LUK.4.29\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Lk 4:29a</a>; 7:12ab; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/JHN.4.8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">J 4:8</a>, 28, 30; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ACT.8.9\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ac 8:9</a>; 14:4; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/REV.11.13\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Rv 11:13</a>; B 16:5; AcPl Ha 4, 18; 5, 17. Igualmente <span class=\"greek\">αἱ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πόλεις</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ACT.16.4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ac 16:4</a>. <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πόλις</span> a cidade pode ser também a capital, a cidade principal (Mayser II/2 p. 28; Jos., C. Ap. 2, 125) <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ACT.8.5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ac 8:5</a>; cf. <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MRK.5.14\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mk 5:14</a> (v. v. 1); <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/LUK.8.27\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Lk 8:27</a> (v. v. 26). <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πόλις</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἐκείνη</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.10.14\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 10:14f</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/LUK.9.5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Lk 9:5</a>; 10:12; 18:3; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/JHN.4.39\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">J 4:39</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ACT.8.8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ac 8:8</a>; Hs 9, 12, 5b. <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πόλ</span>. <span class=\"greek\">αὕτη</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.10.23\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 10:23a</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ACT.4.27\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ac 4:27</a>; 18:10; 22:3; Hs 1:3. <span class=\"greek\">ἔν</span> <span class=\"greek\">τινι</span> <span class=\"greek\">πόλει</span> em certa cidade <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/LUK.18.2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Lk 18:2</a>; cf. Hs 9, 12, 5a. <span class=\"greek\">εἰς</span> <span class=\"greek\">τήνδε</span> <span class=\"greek\">τὴν</span> <span class=\"greek\">πόλιν</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/JAS.4.13\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Js 4:13</a> (v. <span class=\"greek\">ὅδε</span> 2). <span class=\"greek\">πᾶσα</span> <span class=\"greek\">πόλις</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/LUK.10.1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Lk 10:1</a>. <span class=\"greek\">αἱ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πόλεις</span> <span class=\"greek\">πᾶσαι</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.9.35\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 9:35</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ACT.8.40\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ac 8:40</a>; cf. <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MRK.6.33\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mk 6:33</a>.—<span class=\"greek\">πόλις</span> (<span class=\"greek\">πόλεις</span>) ao lado de <span class=\"greek\">κώμη</span> (<span class=\"greek\">κῶμαι</span>) <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.9.35\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 9:35</a>; 10:11; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/LUK.8.1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Lk 8:1</a>; 13:22. Com <span class=\"greek\">κῶμαι</span> e <span class=\"greek\">ἀγροί</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MRK.6.56\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mk 6:56</a>. <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πόλις</span> <span class=\"greek\">καὶ</span> <span class=\"greek\">οἱ</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἀγροί</span> 5:14; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/LUK.8.34\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Lk 8:34</a>. Com <span class=\"greek\">τόπος</span> 10:1. Em contraste com a planície aberta ou o deserto, onde não se encontram cidades <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.14.13\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 14:13</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MRK.1.45\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mk 1:45</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2CO.11.26\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2 Cor 11:26</a>; com o interior de um edifício <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ACT.12.10\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ac 12:10</a>.—Empregado com gen.: para denotar a região em que está situada <span class=\"greek\">πόλ</span>. <span class=\"greek\">τῆς</span> <span class=\"greek\">Γαλιλαίας</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/LUK.1.26\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Lk 1:26</a>; 4:31. <span class=\"greek\">πόλ</span>. <span class=\"greek\">Ἰούδα</span> (<span class=\"greek\">Ἰούδας</span> 1c) 1:39. Cf. <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/JHN.4.5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">J 4:5</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ACT.14.6\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ac 14:6</a>; 21:39; para denotar os habitantes (Diod S 34 e 35 Fgm. 23 <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> <span class=\"greek\">τῶν</span> <span class=\"greek\">Γαλατῶν</span> <span class=\"greek\">πόλις</span>; Jos., Ant. 1, 200) <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πόλ</span>. <span class=\"greek\">Δαμασκηνῶν</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2CO.11.32\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2 Cor 11:32</a>. <span class=\"greek\">π</span>. <span class=\"greek\">Σαμαριτῶν</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.10.5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 10:5</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/LUK.9.52\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Lk 9:52</a> v.l. Cf. 23:51; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ACT.19.35\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ac 19:35</a>; EpilMosq 4; AcPl Ox 6, 20 (=Aa I 242, 1). <span class=\"greek\">αἱ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πόλεις</span> <span class=\"greek\">τοῦ</span> <span class=\"greek\">Ἰσραήλ</span> as cidades em que vive o povo de Israel <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.10.23\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 10:23b</a> (<span class=\"greek\">Ἰσραήλ</span> 2).—<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/REV.16.19\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Rv 16:19b</a>. <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πόλ</span>. <span class=\"greek\">αὐτῶν</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.22.7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 22:7</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/LUK.4.29\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Lk 4:29b</a>.—2:39. Também com gen. sing. <span class=\"greek\">πόλ</span>. <span class=\"greek\">Δαυίδ</span> cidade de Davi 2:4b, 11; <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἑαυτοῦ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πολ</span>. a própria cidade da pessoa (=localidade ancestral; mas 2:39 Nazaré = seu lugar de residência) 2:3.—<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/JHN.1.44\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">J 1:44</a>. Também <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἰδία</span> <span class=\"greek\">πόλ</span>. (v. <span class=\"greek\">ἴδιος</span> 1b) <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.9.1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 9:1</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/LUK.2.3\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Lk 2:3</a> v.l.; Hs 1:2b (em linguagem figurada, v. 2 abaixo). Pl. 1 Cl 55:1. As <span class=\"greek\">πόλεις</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἴδιαι</span> dos cristãos Dg 5:2 são aquelas habitadas exclusivamente por eles; contrastam com <span class=\"greek\">πόλεις</span> <span class=\"greek\">Ἑλληνίδες</span> cidades gregas (cf. SIG 761, 15 [48/47 a.C.]; 909, 2), <span class=\"greek\">π</span>. <span class=\"greek\">βάρβαροι</span> Dg 5:4.—<span class=\"greek\">π</span>. <span class=\"greek\">μεγάλαι</span> grandes cidades 1 Cl 6:4; AcPl Ha 2, 25f. Em Rv <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πόλ</span>. <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span>. <span class=\"greek\">μεγάλη</span> (Tat. 19, 1; 29, 1 Roma) é quase sempre ‘Babilônia’ (v. <span class=\"greek\">Βαβυλών</span>) 16:19a; 17:18; 18:16, 18f, 21; <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πόλις</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> <span class=\"greek\">μεγάλη</span>, <span class=\"greek\">Βαβυλὼν</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πόλις</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἰσχυρά</span> 18:10. Por outro lado, <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πόλ</span>. <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> <span class=\"greek\">μεγάλη</span> 11:8 é claramente Jerusalém (como SibOr 5, 154; 226). Em outros lugares Jerusalém é chamada <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πόλ</span>. <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἠγαπημένη</span> 20:9 (cf. ApcSed 8:3 <span class=\"greek\">πρῶτον</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἠγάπησας</span> … <span class=\"greek\">εἰς</span> <span class=\"greek\">τὰς</span> <span class=\"greek\">πόλεις</span> <span class=\"greek\">τὴν</span> <span class=\"greek\">Ἰερουσαλήμ</span>); <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἁγία</span> <span class=\"greek\">πόλ</span>. <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.4.5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 4:5</a>; 27:53; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/REV.11.2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Rv 11:2</a> (<span class=\"greek\">ἅγιος</span> 1a<span class=\"greek\">α</span>); <span class=\"greek\">πόλ</span>. <span class=\"greek\">τοῦ</span> <span class=\"greek\">μεγάλου</span> <span class=\"greek\">βασιλέως</span> a cidade do Grande Rei <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.5.35\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 5:35</a> (<span class=\"greek\">βασιλεύς</span> 2b). <span class=\"greek\">εἰς</span> <span class=\"greek\">πόλιν</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἄρχουσαν</span> <span class=\"greek\">ὀπύσεως</span> na cidade que promove a fornicação ApcPt Rainer 4, 1 (Ja. p. 278; v. também <span class=\"greek\">ὄπυσις</span>).—O nome da povoação ou cidade que acompanha <span class=\"greek\">πόλις</span> encontra-se ou no gen. epexegético (Aeschyl. et al.; também Demetr.: 722 Fgm. 1, 8 Jac. <span class=\"greek\">πόλιν</span> <span class=\"greek\">Σικίμων</span>) <span class=\"greek\">πόλεις</span> <span class=\"greek\">Σοδόμων</span> <span class=\"greek\">καὶ</span> <span class=\"greek\">Γομόρρας</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2PE.2.6\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2 Pt 2:6</a>, ou no mesmo caso em que se encontra <span class=\"greek\">πόλις</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ἐν</span> <span class=\"greek\">πόλει</span> <span class=\"greek\">Ἰόππῃ</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ACT.11.5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ac 11:5</a>; <span class=\"greek\">πόλις</span> <span class=\"greek\">Λασαία</span> 27:8. Da construção <span class=\"greek\">πόλεως</span> <span class=\"greek\">Θυατίρων</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ACT.16.14\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ac 16:14</a> não se pode determinar o nom. de <span class=\"greek\">Θυ</span>-: ou <span class=\"greek\">πόλις</span> <span class=\"greek\">Θυατίρων</span> ou <span class=\"greek\">πόλις</span> <span class=\"greek\">Θυάτιρα</span> (B-D-R §167, 3). Com topônimos indeclináveis <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/LUK.2.4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Lk 2:4a</a>, 39. <span class=\"greek\">πόλις</span> <span class=\"greek\">λεγομένη</span> ou <span class=\"greek\">καλουμένη</span> seguido do nome <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.2.23\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 2:23</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/LUK.7.11\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Lk 7:11</a>; 9:10. Cf. <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/JHN.11.54\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">J 11:54</a>.—<span class=\"greek\">ἀπὸ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πόλεως</span> <span class=\"greek\">εἰς</span> <span class=\"greek\">πόλιν</span> (Aesop, Fab. 228 P.//421 H.//354 Ch.//H-H. 256 <span class=\"greek\">μεταβαίνουσιν</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἀπὸ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πόλεως</span> <span class=\"greek\">εἰς</span> <span class=\"greek\">πόλιν</span>) <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.23.34\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 23:34</a>. <span class=\"greek\">κατὰ</span> <span class=\"greek\">τὴν</span> <span class=\"greek\">πόλιν</span> em qualquer lugar da cidade <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ACT.24.12\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ac 24:12</a>. Cf. <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/LUK.8.39\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Lk 8:39</a> (<span class=\"greek\">κατά</span> B1a). <span class=\"greek\">κατὰ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πόλιν</span> de cidade em cidade IRo 9:3; pl. <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/LUK.13.22\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Lk 13:22</a>; em cada cidade (Appian, Bell. Civ. 1. 39 §177) <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ACT.15.21\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ac 15:21</a>, 36 (<span class=\"greek\">κατὰ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πόλιν</span> <span class=\"greek\">πᾶσαν</span>); 20:23; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/TIT.1.5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Tit 1:5</a> (Diod S 5, 78, 2 Creta tem, de fato, ‘não poucas’ cidades). Cf. <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/LUK.8.1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Lk 8:1</a>, 4 (<span class=\"greek\">κατά</span> B1d). <span class=\"greek\">αἱ</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἔξω</span> <span class=\"greek\">πόλεις</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ACT.26.11\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ac 26:11</a> (<span class=\"greek\">ἔξω</span> 1a<span class=\"greek\">β</span>). <span class=\"greek\">αἱ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πέριξ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πόλεις</span> 5:16 (v. <span class=\"greek\">πέριξ</span>). <span class=\"greek\">αἱ</span> <span class=\"greek\">περὶ</span> <span class=\"greek\">αὐτὰς</span> (isto é, Sodoma e Gomorra) <span class=\"greek\">πόλεις</span> Jd 7. <span class=\"greek\">πρὸ</span> <span class=\"greek\">τ</span>. <span class=\"greek\">πόλεως</span> (Jos., Bell. 1, 234, Ant. 10, 44) <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ACT.14.13\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ac 14:13</a>.</p><p class=\"entry-text\">② A cidade (celestial) = a Nova Jerusalém (Bousset, Rel.3 283ff; RKnopf, GHeinrici Festschr. 14, 213–19; McQueen, Exp. 9ª série, 2, 1924, 220–26; FDijkema, NThT 15, 1926, 25–43) <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/HEB.11.10\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Hb 11:10</a>, 16 (cf. TestJob 18:8; TestAbr A 2 p. 78, 30 [Stone p. 4] <span class=\"greek\">ἀπὸ</span> <span class=\"greek\">τῆς</span> <span class=\"greek\">μεγάλης</span> <span class=\"greek\">πόλεως</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἔρχομαι</span> [de Miguel]). <span class=\"greek\">πόλ</span>. <span class=\"greek\">θεοῦ</span> <span class=\"greek\">ζῶντος</span> 12:22 (SibOr 5, 250 <span class=\"greek\">θεοῦ</span> <span class=\"greek\">π</span>. acerca de Jerusalém). <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> <span class=\"greek\">μέλλουσα</span> (oposta a <span class=\"greek\">οὐ</span> … <span class=\"greek\">μένουσα</span> <span class=\"greek\">πόλις</span>) 13:14. Especialmente em Rv: <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πόλις</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἁγία</span> <span class=\"greek\">Ἰερουσαλὴμ</span> (<span class=\"greek\">καινή</span>) 21:2, 10 (CBouma, GereformTT 36, ’36, 91–98). Além disso, vv. 14–16, 18f, 21, 23; 22:14, 19; também 3:12. (Cf. a descrição da cidade maravilhosa por Lucian em Ver. Hist. 2, 11f: <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πόλις</span> <span class=\"greek\">πᾶσα</span> <span class=\"greek\">χρυσῆ</span>, <span class=\"greek\">τὸ</span> <span class=\"greek\">τεῖχος</span> <span class=\"greek\">σμαράγδινον</span>. <span class=\"greek\">πύλαι</span> … <span class=\"greek\">ἑπτά</span>, <span class=\"greek\">πᾶσαι</span> <span class=\"greek\">μονόξυλοι</span> <span class=\"greek\">κινναμώμιναι</span> … <span class=\"greek\">γῆ</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἐλεφαντίνη</span> … <span class=\"greek\">ναοὶ</span> <span class=\"greek\">βηρύλλου</span> <span class=\"greek\">λίθου</span> … <span class=\"greek\">βωμοὶ</span> … <span class=\"greek\">ἀμεθύστινοι</span> … <span class=\"greek\">ποταμὸς</span> <span class=\"greek\">μύρου</span> <span class=\"greek\">τοῦ</span> <span class=\"greek\">καλλίστου</span> … <span class=\"greek\">οἶκοι</span> <span class=\"greek\">ὑάλινοι</span> … <span class=\"greek\">οὐδὲ</span> <span class=\"greek\">νὺξ</span> <span class=\"greek\">οὐδὲ</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἡμέρα</span>.) Sobre o tema, v. JMorwood, Aeneas, Augustus, and the Theme of the City: Greece and Rome nova série 38, ’91, 212–23.—Hs 1:1, 2.</p><p class=\"entry-text\">③ Habitantes de uma cidade, cidade, abstrato pelo concreto (X., Cyr. 1, 4, 25; Herodian 3, 2, 7; Jos., Ant. 5, 357) <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/LUK.4.43\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Lk 4:43</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ACT.14.21\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ac 14:21</a>; 16:20 (cf. Jos., Bell. 7, 41; DWhitehead, MusHelv 53/1, ’96, 1–11 [sobre a identificação dos cidadãos e do lugar, cf. Thu. 2, 2, 1; X., Hell. 2, 2, 9]). <span class=\"greek\">πᾶσα</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πόλις</span> (Diod S 18, 70, 2; Appian, Numid. 1) <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.8.34\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 8:34</a>; 21:10 (seguido de <span class=\"greek\">λέγουσα</span>); <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ACT.13.44\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ac 13:44</a>; <span class=\"greek\">ὅλη</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> <span class=\"greek\">π</span>. (Diod S 10, 3, 2) <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MRK.1.33\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mk 1:33</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ACT.21.30\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ac 21:30</a>. <span class=\"greek\">πόλις</span> <span class=\"greek\">μερισθεῖσα</span> <span class=\"greek\">καθ</span>’ <span class=\"greek\">ἑαυτῆς</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.12.25\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 12:25</a>. <span class=\"greek\">ἐθριαμβεύετο</span> <span class=\"greek\">ὑπὸ</span> <span class=\"greek\">τῆς</span> <span class=\"greek\">πόλεως</span> (Paulo) era escarnecido pela cidade AcPl Ha 4, 13 (v. <span class=\"greek\">θριαμβεύω</span> 5). HConn, Lucan Perspective and the City: Missiology 13, ’85, 409–28 (Lk-Ac contém metade das 160+ ocorrências de <span class=\"greek\">π</span>. no NT).—B. 1308. Schmidt, Syn. II 495–507. DELG. M-M. EDNT. TW.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0292-02\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πολιτάρχης, ου, ὁ</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>substantivo masculino</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πολιτάρχης</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ου</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ὁ</span> (sobre a forma, cf. <span class=\"greek\">πολίαρχος</span> Mason 76f; encontrado somente em inscrições e papiros, mas Aeneas Tact. 26, 12 apresenta uma variante dialetal <span class=\"greek\">πολίταρχος</span>), magistrado que fazia parte do conselho de uma povoação ou cidade, autoridade municipal. Não subsiste uma descrição precisa das atribuições, mas a administração das medidas de segurança, conforme indicado por Aeneas Tact. 26, 12 e sugerido pelas circunstâncias registradas em <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ACT.17.5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ac 17:5</a>–13, certamente era atribuída a tal cargo, anterior a 167 a.C. Vários <span class=\"greek\">π</span>. (cinco ou seis em Tessalônica) constituíam o conselho municipal nas cidades macedônicas e ocasionalmente em outras (v. EBurton, The Politarchs in Macedonia and Elsewhere: AJTh 2, 1898, 598–632 com exemplos de inscrições; v. também SIG 700, 1; 48 [a cidade macedônica de Letae, 118/117 a.C.]; POxy 745, 4 [I a.C./I d.C.]; Sb 5765, 7), especificamente em Tessalônica (CIG II 1967; BCH 18, 1894, 420; 21, 1897, 161 e outros; de Bereia SEG XXVII, 261 [II a.C.] <span class=\"greek\">παρὰ</span> <span class=\"greek\">τῶν</span> <span class=\"greek\">πολιταρχῶν</span> <span class=\"greek\">οὐ</span> <span class=\"greek\">εἷς</span>=um voto ‘não’ dentre os politarcas) <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ACT.17.6\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ac 17:6</a>, 8.—Inscrições em IMakedD; EBurton, AJT 2, 1898, 598–632; Ferguson, Legal Terms 65f e índice, p. 103 com referências a Demitsas; CSchuler, ClPh 55, ’60, 90–100 [com lista de todas as inscrições então conhecidas referentes à Macedônia, a maioria de Tessalônica]; JOliver, ClPh 58, ’63, 164f; Pauly-W., Suppl. 13, ’73, 483–500; BLaourdas/CMakaronas, eds., Ancient Macedonia II ’77, 139–50 [JCormack, ‘Gymnasiarchal Law of Beroea’], 531–44 [BHelly, ‘Politarques, Poliarques et Polito-phylaques’]; MHatzopoulos, em Dritter internationaler Thrakologischer Kongress zu Ehren WTomascheks, 2–6 Juni 1980, ’84, 137–49; GHorsley, ABD V, 384–89, com lista de inscrições e bibliografia; Boffo, Iscrizioni n. 27 (bibliografia); Hemer Acts 115; v. também New Docs, ’82, 34f; SEG XLIV, 499.—V. DELG s.v. <span class=\"greek\">ἄρχω</span> C. M-M.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0292-03\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πολιτεία, ας, ἡ</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>substantivo feminino</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πολιτεία</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ας</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> (<span class=\"greek\">πολίτης</span>; Hdt.+; inscrições, papiros; 2, 3, 4 Macc; TestAbr A 20 p. 104, 7 [Stone p. 56]; ApcMos prol.; Philo, Joseph., Just., Tat.)</p><p class=\"entry-text\">① Direito de ser membro de uma entidade sociopolítica, cidadania (Hdt. 9, 34; X., Hell. 1, 1, 26; 1, 2, 10; 4, 4, 6; Polyb. 6, 2, 12; Diod S 14, 8, 3; 14, 17, 3; Cyr. Ins. 57; 59; Gnomon [=BGU V 1] 47; 3 Macc 3:21, 23; Jos., Ant. 12, 119), lit., acerca da cidadania romana (Dio Chrys. 24 [41], 2 <span class=\"greek\">Ῥωμαίων</span> <span class=\"greek\">π</span>.; Ael. Aristid. 30, 10 K.=10 p. 117 D.; IG IV2/1, 84, 33 [40/42 d.C.]; Jos., Bell. 1, 194 e Vi 423 <span class=\"greek\">π</span>. <span class=\"greek\">Ῥωμαίων</span>.—WRamsay, The Social Basis of Roman Power in Asia Minor ’41) <span class=\"greek\">πολιτείαν</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἐκτησάμην</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ACT.22.28\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ac 22:28</a>.—Em sentido transferido, esta tradução é possível (EHaupt, PEwald et al.) para <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/EPH.2.12\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Eph 2:12</a>, mas não muito provável (v. 2 abaixo).</p><p class=\"entry-text\">② Unidade sociopolítica ou corpo de cidadãos, Estado, povo, corpo político (Thu. 1, 127, 3; Pla., Rep. 10, 619c; Diod S 5, 45, 3; Appian, Bell. Civ. 2, 19 §68; Just., A II, 10, 6) <span class=\"greek\">ἀπηλλοτριωμένοι</span> <span class=\"greek\">τ</span>. <span class=\"greek\">πολιτείας</span> <span class=\"greek\">τοῦ</span> <span class=\"greek\">Ἰσραήλ</span> alheios ao povo de Israel <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/EPH.2.12\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Eph 2:12</a> (assim HvSoden, MDibelius, NRSV et al.; v. 1 acima).</p><p class=\"entry-text\">③ Comportamento conforme os padrões esperados de um cidadão respeitável, modo de vida, conduta (Athen. 1, 19a; Herm. Wr. em Stob. p. 486, 24 Sc. <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> <span class=\"greek\">τῶν</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἀνθρώπων</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἄγριος</span> <span class=\"greek\">πολιτεία</span>; Ps.-Liban., Charact. Ep. p. 34, 2; 47, 8; 10; Biogr. p. 261; TestAbr A 20 p. 104, 7 [Stone p. 56]; ApcMos prol.; Just., A I, 4, 2 e outros; Tat.) Dg 5:4; <span class=\"greek\">ἀγαθὴ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πολ</span>. MPol 13:2; <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἀπ</span>’ <span class=\"greek\">ἀρχῆς</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἀνεπίληπτος</span> <span class=\"greek\">πολ</span>. 17:1; <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πανάρετος</span> <span class=\"greek\">καὶ</span> <span class=\"greek\">σεβάσμιος</span> <span class=\"greek\">πολ</span>. 1 Cl 2:8. <span class=\"greek\">οἱ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πολιτευόμενοι</span> <span class=\"greek\">τὴν</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἀμεταμέλητον</span> <span class=\"greek\">πολιτείαν</span> <span class=\"greek\">τοῦ</span> <span class=\"greek\">θεοῦ</span> aqueles que seguem o modo de vida de Deus, que não traz motivos de pesar 54:4 (<span class=\"greek\">πολιτεύεσθαι</span> <span class=\"greek\">πολιτείαν</span> em Nicol. Dam.: 90 Fgm. 126 Jac. e na inscrição da sinagoga de Stobi [c. 100 d.C.] linhas 6f: ZNW 32, ’33, 93f).—DELG s.v. <span class=\"greek\">πόλις</span>. M-M. TW. Spicq.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0292-04\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πολίτευμα, ατος, τό</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>substantivo neutro</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πολίτευμα</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ατος</span>, <span class=\"greek\">τό</span> (<span class=\"greek\">πολίτης</span>, cf. o artigo anterior e o seguinte; Pla. et al.; inscrições, papiros), comunidade política, Estado (assim Polyb. 1, 13, 12; 35, 5; Diod S 19, 75, 4; inscrições; 2 Macc 12:7; Jos., Ant. 1, 13, C. Ap. 2, 257; fig. Philo, Agr. 81 <span class=\"greek\">τῷ</span> <span class=\"greek\">τῆς</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἀρετῆς</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἐγγεγραμμέναι</span> <span class=\"greek\">πολιτεύματι</span>, Conf. Lingu. 78 <span class=\"greek\">πατρίδα</span> <span class=\"greek\">τὸν</span> <span class=\"greek\">οὐράνιον</span> <span class=\"greek\">χῶρον</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἐν</span> <span class=\"greek\">ᾧ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πολιτεύονται</span>.—Schürer III 88f; PBöttger, ZNW 60, ’69, 244–53) <span class=\"greek\">ἡμῶν</span> <span class=\"greek\">τὸ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πολ</span>. <span class=\"greek\">ἐν</span> <span class=\"greek\">οὐρανοῖς</span> <span class=\"greek\">ὑπάρχει</span> nossa comunidade política está no céu <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/PHP.3.20\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Phil 3:20</a> (<span class=\"greek\">πολίτευμα</span> frequentemente designa uma colônia de estrangeiros ou de veteranos reassentados CIG 5361, III add. 5866c; PTebt 32, 9; 17 [II a.C.]; EpArist 310. Cf. OGI 737, 2 com nota 2 e a bibliografia em MDibelius, Hdb. ad loc.; JdeZwaan, Philippenzen 3:20 en de <span class=\"greek\">Κοινή</span>: TSt 31, 1913, 298–300; LFuchs, D. Juden in Ägypten 1924, 89; MEngers, <span class=\"greek\">Πολίτευμα</span>: Mnemosyne 54, 1926, 154–61; WRuppel, Politeuma: Philol. 82, 1927, 268–312; 433–52; EPeterson s.v. <span class=\"greek\">ἐκκλησία</span>, fim; ‘Nossa pátria está no céu, e aqui na terra somos uma colônia de cidadãos celestiais’ MDibelius.—O sentido parece ser mais geral em Menand. Rhet. [II d.C.] III 421, 16 Spengel: o falecido, segundo a palavra de consolação, <span class=\"greek\">πολιτεύεται</span> <span class=\"greek\">μετὰ</span> <span class=\"greek\">τῶν</span> <span class=\"greek\">θεῶν</span>; Hierocles, 3, 2 p. 424: ‘heróis’ conduzem as almas dos justos <span class=\"greek\">πρὸς</span> <span class=\"greek\">τὴν</span> <span class=\"greek\">θείαν</span> <span class=\"greek\">πολιτείαν</span>. Olympiodorus In Platonis Phaedonem, ed. WNorvin 1913 p. 122, 8 [sobre Pla., Phd. 69c] acerca do filósofo: <span class=\"greek\">συμπολιτεύεσθαι</span> <span class=\"greek\">τοῖς</span> <span class=\"greek\">θεοῖς</span> <span class=\"greek\">καὶ</span> <span class=\"greek\">συνοικονομεῖν</span>).—DELG s.v. <span class=\"greek\">πόλις</span>. M-M. TW. Spicq. Sv.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0292-05\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πολιτεύομαι</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>verbo</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πολιτεύομαι</span> (<span class=\"greek\">πολίτης</span>; a voz méd., única encontrada em nossa literatura, desde Thu., Aristoph.+) 1º aor. <span class=\"greek\">ἐπολιτευσάμην</span>, subj. 1ª pess. pl. <span class=\"greek\">πολιτευσώμεθα</span>; perf. <span class=\"greek\">πεπολίτευμαι</span>.</p><p class=\"entry-text\">① Ser cidadão, ter sua cidadania/pátria (Philo, Conf. Lingu. 78 [v. <span class=\"greek\">πολίτευμα</span>]), acerca dos cristãos <span class=\"greek\">ἐν</span> <span class=\"greek\">οὐρανῷ</span> Dg 5:9 (Himerius, Or. 8 [=23], 23 acerca de um falecido: <span class=\"greek\">μετὰ</span> <span class=\"greek\">θεῶν</span> <span class=\"greek\">πολιτεύεσθαι</span>; Hippol., Ref. 6, 34, 3 acerca dos anjos: <span class=\"greek\">π</span>. <span class=\"greek\">ἐν</span> <span class=\"greek\">Ἱερουσαλὴμ</span> <span class=\"greek\">τῇ</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἄνω</span>; cf. Iren. 4, 5, 3 [Harv. II 156, 8; aqui oposto a <span class=\"greek\">ξενιτεύω</span> ‘viver longe da pátria’]).</p><p class=\"entry-text\">② Administrar um corpo constituído, reger</p><p class=\"entry-text\">ⓐ De um chefe de Estado, governar um Estado, uso absoluto (Thu. 2, 15, 1 e outros; Jos., Ant. 14, 91 <span class=\"greek\">π</span>. <span class=\"greek\">ἐν</span> <span class=\"greek\">Ἱερος</span>.) acerca de Deus, que <span class=\"greek\">ἐν</span> <span class=\"greek\">οὐρανοῖς</span> <span class=\"greek\">πολιτεύεται</span> governa no céu Dg 10:7.</p><p class=\"entry-text\">ⓑ De autoridades eclesiásticas (Orig., C. Cels. 3, 30, 15) 1 Cl 44:6.</p><p class=\"entry-text\">③ Conduzir a própria vida, viver, levar a vida (UPZ 144, 14 [164/163 a.C.] <span class=\"greek\">ὁσίως</span> <span class=\"greek\">κ</span>. <span class=\"greek\">δικαίως</span>; Hierocles 11, 444; Ps.-Liban., Charact. Ep. p. 31, 5 <span class=\"greek\">σεμνῶς</span>; 34, 1; 2 Macc 6:1; 11:25; 3 Macc 3:4; 4 Macc 2:8 e outros; ApcEsdr 2:9; Philo, Virt. 161, Spec. Leg. 4, 226; Jos., Ant. 12, 142, Vi. 12; Just., Tat., Ath.; Did., Gen. 153, 28 <span class=\"greek\">καλῶς</span>) <span class=\"greek\">καλῶς</span> <span class=\"greek\">κ</span>. <span class=\"greek\">ἁγνῶς</span> Hs 5, 6, 6. <span class=\"greek\">ὁσίως</span> 1 Cl 6:1. <span class=\"greek\">ἀξίως</span> <span class=\"greek\">τινός</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/PHP.1.27\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Phil 1:27</a> (RBrewer, JBL 73, ’54, 76–83: ‘cumpri vossas obrigações como cidadãos’; EMiller, JSNT 15, ’82, 86–96; EKrentz, em Origins and Method, JHurd Festschr., ed. BMcLean ’93, 114–17); 1 Cl 21:1; Pol 5:2. <span class=\"greek\">μετὰ</span> <span class=\"greek\">φόβου</span> <span class=\"greek\">καὶ</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἀγάπης</span> 1 Cl 51:2. (Com <span class=\"greek\">πορεύεσθαι</span>) <span class=\"greek\">πολιτεύεσθαι</span> <span class=\"greek\">κατὰ</span> <span class=\"greek\">τὸ</span> <span class=\"greek\">καθῆκον</span> <span class=\"greek\">τῷ</span> <span class=\"greek\">Χριστῷ</span> 3:4 (<span class=\"greek\">πολ</span>. <span class=\"greek\">κατά</span> <span class=\"greek\">τι</span> como SIG 618, 12 [188 a.C.]; 2 Macc 11:25; 4 Macc 2:23; EpArist 31; Jos., Ant. 12, 142; Did., Gen. 196, 29); <span class=\"greek\">π</span>. <span class=\"greek\">πολιτείαν</span> 54:4 (<span class=\"greek\">πολιτεία</span> 3). Com duplo dat. <span class=\"greek\">συνειδήσει</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἀγαθῇ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πεπολίτευμαι</span> <span class=\"greek\">τῷ</span> <span class=\"greek\">θεῷ</span> tenho vivido com consciência limpa perante Deus <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ACT.23.1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ac 23:1</a> (para o dat. <span class=\"greek\">τῷ</span> <span class=\"greek\">θεῷ</span> cf. PHib 63, 10 [III a.C.] <span class=\"greek\">εἰ</span> <span class=\"greek\">οὕτως</span> <span class=\"greek\">πολιτευσόμεθα</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἀλλήλοις</span>).—Straub p. 30. DELG s.v. <span class=\"greek\">πόλις</span>. M-M. TW. Spicq. Sv.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0292-06\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πολίτης, ου, ὁ</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>substantivo masculino</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πολίτης</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ου</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ὁ</span> (<span class=\"greek\">πόλις</span>; Hom. et al.; inscrições, papiros, LXX, TestJob 29, 1; EpArist, Philo, Joseph.)</p><p class=\"entry-text\">① Aquele que vive em uma cidade ou país ou deles procede, cidadão de <span class=\"greek\">πόλεως</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ACT.21.39\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ac 21:39</a>. <span class=\"greek\">τῆς</span> <span class=\"greek\">χώρας</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἐκείνης</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/LUK.15.15\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Lk 15:15</a>. (Oposto a <span class=\"greek\">ξένοι</span>, como Philo, Poster. Cai. 109) Dg 5:5; AcPl Ha 4, 6.</p><p class=\"entry-text\">② Membro do próprio grupo sociopolítico, concidadão, compatriota (Pla., Apol. 37c, Prot. 339f; Diod S 11, 47, 3; 11, 62, 1 e outros; Phlegon: 257 Fgm. 36, 2, 4 Jac.; Appian, Bell. Civ. 4, 127 §531 e outros; Chion, Ep. 15, 1; Pr 11:9; 24:28; TestJob 29:1; Jos., Ant. 1, 21, Vi. 274) <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/HEB.8.11\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Hb 8:11</a> (Jer 38:34). Os compatriotas ou súditos de um governante são igualmente assim denominados (escol. sobre Nicander, Ther. 15 [p. 5, 34]; Jos., Ant. 12, 162) 1 Cl 55:1. Cf. <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/LUK.19.14\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Lk 19:14</a>.—DELG s.v. <span class=\"greek\">πόλις</span>. M-M. TW. Spicq.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0292-07\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πολῖτις, ιδος, ἡ</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>substantivo feminino</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πολῖτις</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ιδος</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> fem. de <span class=\"greek\">πολίτη</span> (Soph., Eur., Pla.; também Menand., Sicyonius 197 S.; inscrições, Philo, Joseph.), cidadã, acerca de Artemila <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> <span class=\"greek\">τῆ</span> <span class=\"greek\">τρυφῆ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πολλῆ</span> <span class=\"greek\">π</span>. cidadã de grande luxo AcPl Ha 2, 19f.—DELG s.v. <span class=\"greek\">πόλις</span>.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0292-08\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πολλά</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>remissão</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πολλά</span> v. <span class=\"greek\">πολύς</span> 1a<span class=\"greek\">β</span>ב.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0292-09\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πολλάκις</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>advérbio</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πολλάκις</span> adv. (Hom.+), relativo a diversos momentos relacionados, muitas vezes, amiúde, frequentemente <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.17.15\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 17:15</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MRK.5.4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mk 5:4</a>; 9:22; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/JHN.18.2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">J 18:2</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ACT.26.11\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ac 26:11</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ROM.1.13\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ro 1:13</a>; 15:22 v.l.; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2CO.11.23\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2 Cor 11:23</a>, 26, 27ab; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/PHP.3.18\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Phil 3:18</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2TI.1.16\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2 Ti 1:16</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/HEB.6.7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Hb 6:7</a>; 9:25f; 10:11; Hv 3, 1, 2. Em jogo de palavras (Dio Chrys. 11 [12], 50; 71; Theodor. Prodr. 6, 93 H. <span class=\"greek\">πολλοῖς</span> <span class=\"greek\">πολλαχοῦ</span> <span class=\"greek\">κ</span>. <span class=\"greek\">πολλάκις</span>; SIG 888, 138f <span class=\"greek\">πολλοὶ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πολλάκις</span> <span class=\"greek\">στρατιῶται</span>; Esth 8:12e <span class=\"greek\">πολλάκις</span> <span class=\"greek\">δὲ</span> <span class=\"greek\">καὶ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πολλοὺς</span> <span class=\"greek\">κτλ</span>.; Jos., C. Ap. 2, 219; 231) <span class=\"greek\">ἐν</span> <span class=\"greek\">πολλοῖς</span> <span class=\"greek\">πολλάκις</span> frequentemente de muitas maneiras <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2CO.8.22\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2 Cor 8:22</a> (<span class=\"greek\">πολύ</span> e <span class=\"greek\">πολλῇ</span> seguem-se na mesma oração).—B. 986. M-M.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0292-10\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πολλαπλασιάζω</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>verbo</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πολλαπλασιάζω</span> (<span class=\"greek\">πολύ</span>, <span class=\"greek\">πλάσσω</span>; Aristot., Ph. 237b, 33; Polyb. 30, 4, 13; Diod S 1, 1, et al.), multiplicar, aumentar <span class=\"greek\">π</span>. <span class=\"greek\">τὴν</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἐργασίαν</span> aumentar os rendimentos (=obter muito lucro de um investimento) GHb 297, 21.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0292-11\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πολλαπλασίων, ον,</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>adjetivo</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πολλαπλασίων</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ον</span>, gen. <span class=\"greek\">ονος</span> (Isocr. 15, 177; Archimed. II 134, 13 Heib.; Polyb. 35, 4, 4; Philodem., <span class=\"greek\">Π</span>. <span class=\"greek\">σημ</span>. 9, 32; Plut., Mor. 191c; 215b; Jos., Bell. 1, 514; Ael. Aristid. 27, 20 K.=16 p. 390 D. em lugar do anterior <span class=\"greek\">πολλαπλάσιος</span> [Hdt., Pla. et al.; assim também Philo, Somn. 1, 53; Jos., Bell. 5, 553]), muito acima de uma quantidade normalmente esperada, muitas vezes mais, multiplicado <span class=\"greek\">λαμβάνειν</span> neut. pl. <span class=\"greek\">πολλαπλασίονα</span> (Jos., Bell. 1, 514; TestZeb 6:6) <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.19.29\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 19:29</a> v.l.; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/LUK.18.30\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Lk 18:30</a>.—ESchwyzer, Museum Helveticum 2, ’45, 137–47; Renehan ’75, 167.—M-M.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0292-12\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πολλοστός, ή, όν</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>adjetivo</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πολλοστός</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ή</span>, <span class=\"greek\">όν</span> formado de <span class=\"greek\">πολύς</span> por analogia com <span class=\"greek\">εἰκοστός</span> (v. L-S-J-M; Schwyzer I 584.—No grego não bíblico, frequente em referência ao afastamento relativo em uma escala de extensão ou grau Aristoph., X., Pla.; Philo, De Somn. 1, 204, De Praem. 128; <span class=\"greek\">πολλοστὸν</span> <span class=\"greek\">μέρος</span> ‘menor parte’ ou ‘fração muito pequena’ Andoc. et al. Empregado como <span class=\"greek\">πολύς</span> para denotar grau 2 Km 23:20 <span class=\"greek\">πολλοστός</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἔργοις</span>=‘notável por muitos feitos’; Ps 54:19 Sym.; cf. Pr 5:19), abundante, acerca do corpo ressuscitado (na imagem de um grão de trigo) <span class=\"greek\">σῶμα</span> … <span class=\"greek\">π</span>., <span class=\"greek\">ὀρθόν</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ηὐλογημένον</span> um corpo … abundante/exuberante (porque é produtivo), ereto e abençoado AcPlCor 2:27.—DELG s.v. <span class=\"greek\">πολύς</span>.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0292-13\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πόλος, ου, ὁ</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>substantivo masculino</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πόλος</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ου</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ὁ</span> (<span class=\"greek\">πέλομαι</span> ‘tornar-se, ser’; Aeschyl., Hdt., Pla. et al.; Philo; Jos., Ant. 3, 184), abóbada celeste, firmamento <span class=\"greek\">ἀνέβλεψα</span> <span class=\"greek\">εἰς</span> <span class=\"greek\">τὸν</span> <span class=\"greek\">π</span>. olhei para o firmamento GJs 18:2 (códices).—DELG s.v. <span class=\"greek\">πέλομαι</span>.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0292-14\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πολυαγάπητος, ον</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>adjetivo</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πολυαγάπητος</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ον</span> (Hesychius s.v. <span class=\"greek\">πολύθεστος</span>), muito amado <span class=\"greek\">ὄνομα</span> IEph 1:1.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0292-15\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">Πολύβιος, ου, ὁ</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>nome próprio masculino</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">Πολύβιος</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ου</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ὁ</span> (Dit., Syll. 686; 1115, 30), Políbio, bispo de Trales ITr 1:1.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0292-16\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πολυευσπλαγχνία, ας, ἡ</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>substantivo feminino</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πολυευσπλαγχνία</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ας</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> (cf. <span class=\"greek\">πολυεύσπλαγχνος</span>), abundância de misericórdia <span class=\"greek\">π</span>. <span class=\"greek\">τοῦ</span> <span class=\"greek\">κυρίου</span> Hs 8, 6, 1 v.l.—DELG s.v. <span class=\"greek\">σπλήν</span>.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0292-17\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πολυεύσπλαγχνος, ον</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>adjetivo</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πολυεύσπλαγχνος</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ον</span> rico em compaixão, acerca de Deus <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/JAS.5.11\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Js 5:11</a> v.l.; Hs 5, 4, 4.—DELG s.v. <span class=\"greek\">σπλήν</span>.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0292-18\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πολυεύτακτος, ον</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>adjetivo</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πολυεύτακτος</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ον</span> muito bem ordenado/disciplinado, substantivado <span class=\"greek\">ὑμῶν</span> <span class=\"greek\">τὸ</span> <span class=\"greek\">π</span>. <span class=\"greek\">τῆς</span> <span class=\"greek\">κατὰ</span> <span class=\"greek\">θεὸν</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἀγάπης</span> quão bem ordenado é vosso amor semelhante ao de Deus IMg 1:1.—DELG s.v. <span class=\"greek\">τάσσω</span>.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0292-19\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">Πολύκαρπος, ου, ὁ</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>nome próprio masculino</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">Πολύκαρπος</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ου</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ὁ</span> (referências para o nome no Hdb. sobre Pol ins), Policarpo, bispo de Esmirna e, segundo Irineu (3, 3, 4 [Harv. II 12–15]), discípulo do apóstolo João. Morreu como mártir, provavelmente em 22 de fevereiro de 156 d.C. (assim ESchwartz, De Pionio et Polycarpo 1905, Christl. und jüd. Ostertafeln: AGG n.s. VIII 6 [1905] 125ff). Outros cálculos concluem que a data é 23 de fevereiro de 155 ou 166 d.C. (v. Harnack, Chronologie I 1897, 325ff; PCorssen, ZNW 3, 1902, 61ff; NBonwetsch, RE XV 1904, 535ff). Possuímos uma carta aos filipenses escrita por ele (Pol.—V. PHarrison, Polycarp’s Two Epistles to the Philippians ’36 [bibliografia]); MPol é um relato contemporâneo de seu martírio. IEph 21:1; IMg 15; IPol ins; 7:2; 8:2; Pol ins; MPol 1:1 e outros. Segundo Iren., Eus. e Filipe de Side (na Panfília), Papias foi seu contemporâneo: Papias (1:4; 11:1).—RGrant, Polycarp of Smyrna: ATR 28, ’46, 137–48; Altaner/Stuiber, Patrologie8 ’78 (bibliografia); Pauly-W. XXI 1662–93; Kl. Pauly IV 998f; BHHW III 1479; ABD V 389f.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0292-20\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πολύλαλος, ον</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>adjetivo</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πολύλαλος</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ον</span> (Cleobulus [VI a.C.] em Stob. III p. 112, 3 H.; Ael. Dion. <span class=\"greek\">κ</span>, 8; Vi. Aesopi G 26 P.; escol. sobre Soph., Ant. 324 p. 234 Papag.; Plotinus 6, 2, 21; Job 11:2 Sym.), dado a muita conversa sem propósito, falador, tagarela, com <span class=\"greek\">ἀναιδής</span> Hm 11:12. VandeSande Bakhuyzen suspeita que <span class=\"greek\">πολύλαλοι</span> tenha sido outrora lido em <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/JAS.3.1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Js 3:1</a> em lugar de <span class=\"greek\">πολλοὶ</span> <span class=\"greek\">διδάσκαλοι</span> (B-D-F §115, 1).—DELG s.v. <span class=\"greek\">λαλέω</span>.</p></section></article>"};
